Kernel is configured and compiled with minimal setup, only thing I
changed was to disable unnecessary SCSI drivers and enable the one for
Formac ProRaid lite (Advansys).  Driver for on-board NCR/Symbios SCSI
is enabled since I want to use it as well.

System is Debian GNU/Linux 2.2r4 with Linux 2.4.16 on AXPpci.  Current
MILO (2.0.35-c7b) cannot see any disk devices on either on-board SCSI
if I connect disk device to Advansys adapter.  Devices such as DAT
drive or CD-RW drive connected to Advansys adapter do not cause
problems with MILO and work fine after kernel detects them.  So I
needed to add Advansys driver to MILO and it seems to me that newer
MILO might work if the linking would not fail.

Oh yes, I did disabled ReiserFS support on MILO since my kernel does
not have that driver and I do not need it for now anyway.

