Paavo Hartikainen <pahartik@sci.fi> wrote:
> First I used the cdrecord version on Potato,
> then tried the version on Woody but neither worked.

If you would say what precisely hides behind "neither worked" then
probably you would get some help a long time ago.  My guess would be
that you have problems with a fifo size for which cdrecord wants, by
default, 4 Megs of memory and which is tad too much for "out-of-the-box"
2.2 kernels on Alpha.  There are _many_ ways to change that and quite a
few (at least three, IIRC) are actually described, rather clearly, in
cdrecord documentation.  Probably the easiest way is to put slightly
lower value in a cdrecord configuration file (TFM has a precise syntax
which I do not remember) and forget about the issue.  For the record,
4000k instead of a default 4M works just dandy.

That tidbit of information was posted over years in this newsgroup a
number of times already.

Not that I want to dissuade you from hacking 2.4 kernels but let's
be clear about the issues.

  Michal


