The following syntax has worked for me with both 2.2 and 2.4
kernels, for data and audio (with -pad added for audio):

        cdrecord -v fs=4000k ...

I'm told you can put the "4000k" in the /etc/cdrecord.conf, but
putting the above in a script is pretty easy.

