RAM should be ECC, but some have reported that plain pc100 memory worked.
SCSI can be whatever in most things, but if SRM/ARC/AlphaBIOS doesn't 
recognize it then you can't boot from there.

You could do this, if mobo doesn't contain any kind of disk controller 
then get supported one, Qlogic and Adaptec SCSI are just fine.
Or if  mobo has IDE then plug some ide disk onto it and boot from there 
and continue to scsi disk.

eg. my system goes like this:
 -booting milo from IDE disk
 -milo has support for Adaptec2940 so I can boot from there.

But I could boot it right from SCSI 'cause Alphabios knows it...

-
If you have mobo with only isa & pci then you can forget NVidia based 
graphics cards, they won't work. (bios emulating problem)

