Hi!

I had the same problem with Redhat. I used the jumpstart CD and wrote down
the right way of booting the install from CD, as suggested by jumpstart upon
exiting:
boot dka600 -fi kernels/generic.gz -fl "root=/dev/scd0 bootdevice=scd0"
DKA600 is my CDrom, so replace it with the correct drive as seen by the SRM
console. The quotes must be there as i wrote down (fl "root.........)

For me this worked perfect.

Good luck.
Harry

